      "textEn": "17\n\nIt is a relationship, therefore, while pleading for the special grace of God, they add the prefix 'vi' with the word 'vinit'. Brahmaji is called Aja because he is not born from any mother but directly from the body of God.\nHe is born. As Srila Prabhupada wrote in \"Bhagavan Shri Krishna\", \"This is the conclusion that arises from this,\nthat Narayana is the mother of Brahma.\"For these very reasons, Brahmaji, for his offenses,\nmakes special requests for forgiveness. Narayana, you are not of all the gods,\nThe soul is the witness of all the worlds.\nNarayano angam narabhujalayana-\nTattvam na tavaiva maya. 14>. Meaning of the word:\n\nNarayanah—Lord Narayana; Tvam—You; Na—Not; Hi—What; Sarva—All; Dehinam—Of the embodied beings; Atma—Soul;\nAsi—Be; Adhishadh—He who is the supreme controller; Akhil—Complete; Lok—Of the worlds; Sakshi—Witness; Narayanah—Shri Narayana;\nAngam—Part; Nara—From God; Bhoo—Having emerged; Jal—Of the water; Ayanat—Being the source that manifests; Tat—That part;\nCha—And; Api—Indeed; Satyam—Truth; Na—Not; Tava—Yours; Eva—Even a little; Maya—Illusory power. Hey supreme controller, being the soul of every embodied being and the eternal witness of all the worlds,\nwhy are you not the original Narayan? Undoubtedly, Lord Narayan is a part of you, and he\nis called Narayan because he is the father of the primordial waters of the universe. They are truth, yours\nare not born from illusion.\nMeaning: Srila Prabhupada has commented on this verse in Chaitanya Charitamrita (Adi Lila 2.30) as follows:\nThis is the statement of Brahma, when he was defeated and was praising Lord Krishna after the manifestation of his yogic power. Brahma wanted to test Lord Krishna to see\nwhether Krishna, who plays as a cowherd, is truly God. Brahma stole all the other\nchildren and their cows from the pasture, but when they returned, they saw that all the children and\ncows were in the pasture because God had created them again. When Brahma saw this yogic power of Lord Krishna,\nhe gave up and addressed Lord as his master and the creator of the universe,\nas the seer of every object and the Supreme Being residing within all beings, and\npraised him. Lord Krishna is Narayana, that is, the father of Brahma, because he is the embryo-bearing one in the form of a part of Krishna"
